/**
* Example 39: Reasoning — Enabling It & Reading It Back
*
* Several providers can run an internal reasoning/thinking pass before producing their
* final answer. bx-ai normalizes that reasoning onto the SAME envelope regardless of which
* provider you're on:
*   - Non-streaming: choices[1].message.reasoning  (use options.returnFormat: "raw")
*   - Streaming:     chunk.choices?.first()?.delta?.reasoning
*
* Enabling reasoning is provider-specific and goes in `params`:
*   - Claude:  params: { thinking: { type: "enabled", budget_tokens: 10000 } }
*   - OpenAI:  params: { reasoning_effort: "high" }   (low | medium | high)
*
* Whatever the provider calls it natively (thinking, reasoning_content, etc.), bx-ai maps it
* onto that one standard `reasoning` key so your code doesn't branch per provider. Absence is
* normal — a non-reasoning model, or a provider that never enabled it for the request, simply
* has no `reasoning` key, so always read it with `?: ""`.
*
* Parts 1 & 2 below call REAL providers and need a real API key (CLAUDE_API_KEY /
* OPENAI_API_KEY) to actually execute — they're wrapped in try/catch and print a friendly
* skip message without one. Parts 3 & 4 run fully offline against the "mock" provider (which
* honors a scripted `reasoning` key the same way every real provider's normalized output
* does), so the READING side of this example is always runnable with no API key at all.
*
* What you'll learn:
* - Enabling extended thinking on Claude via params.thinking
* - Enabling reasoning effort on OpenAI via params.reasoning_effort
* - Reading result.choices[1].message.reasoning synchronously (returnFormat: "raw")
* - Reading chunk.choices?.first()?.delta?.reasoning while streaming
*
* Run:
*   boxlang examples/39-reasoning.bxs
*/
println( "========================================" )
println( "Example 39: Reasoning" )
println( "========================================" )
println( "" )

// ============================================================================
// Example 1: Enabling Reasoning on Claude — params.thinking
// ============================================================================
println( "--- Example 1: Claude Extended Thinking ---" )
println( "" )

try {
    claudeResult = aiChat(
        "A farmer has 17 sheep. All but 9 die. How many are left? Show your reasoning.",
        {
            thinking: { type: "enabled", budget_tokens: 10000 }
        },
        { provider: "claude", returnFormat: "raw" }
    )
    claudeReasoning = claudeResult.choices[ 1 ].message.reasoning ?: ""
    claudeAnswer    = claudeResult.choices[ 1 ].message.content ?: ""
    println( "Reasoning: " & claudeReasoning )
    println( "Answer   : " & claudeAnswer )
} catch ( any e ) {
    println( "Skipped (needs CLAUDE_API_KEY): " & e.message )
}
println( "" )

// ============================================================================
// Example 2: Enabling Reasoning on OpenAI — params.reasoning_effort
// ============================================================================
println( "--- Example 2: OpenAI Reasoning Effort ---" )
println( "" )

try {
    openaiResult = aiChat(
        "A farmer has 17 sheep. All but 9 die. How many are left? Show your reasoning.",
        {
            reasoning_effort: "high"
        },
        { provider: "openai", returnFormat: "raw" }
    )
    openaiReasoning = openaiResult.choices[ 1 ].message.reasoning ?: ""
    openaiAnswer    = openaiResult.choices[ 1 ].message.content ?: ""
    println( "Reasoning: " & openaiReasoning )
    println( "Answer   : " & openaiAnswer )
} catch ( any e ) {
    println( "Skipped (needs OPENAI_API_KEY): " & e.message )
}
println( "" )

// ============================================================================
// Example 3: Reading Reasoning Synchronously — the Normalized Envelope, Offline
// ============================================================================
println( "--- Example 3: Reading message.reasoning (offline, deterministic) ---" )
println( "" )

// The mock provider honors a scripted "reasoning" key on the normalized message.reasoning
// key — the exact same key every real reasoning-capable provider's response is mapped onto.
mockReasoningResult = aiChat(
    "A farmer has 17 sheep. All but 9 die. How many are left?",
    {},
    {
        provider       : "mock",
        returnFormat   : "raw",
        providerOptions: {
            responses: [
                {
                    content  : "9 sheep are left.",
                    reasoning: 'The phrase "All but 9 die" means 9 survive — the other details (starting count, cause of death) are irrelevant to the answer.'
                }
            ]
        }
    }
)

reasoning = mockReasoningResult.choices[ 1 ].message.reasoning ?: ""
answer    = mockReasoningResult.choices[ 1 ].message.content ?: ""
println( "Reasoning: " & reasoning )
println( "Answer   : " & answer )
println( "" )
println( "Same read on a model with reasoning disabled — reasoning key is simply absent:" )
noReasoningResult = aiChat( "Say hello.", {}, {
    provider       : "mock",
    returnFormat   : "raw",
    providerOptions: { responses: [ "Hello!" ] }
} )
println( "reasoning ?: '' -> '" & ( noReasoningResult.choices[ 1 ].message.reasoning ?: "" ) & "' (empty, not an error)" )
println( "" )

// ============================================================================
// Example 4: Reading Reasoning While Streaming — delta.reasoning
// ============================================================================
println( "--- Example 4: Reading delta.reasoning while streaming (offline, deterministic) ---" )
println( "" )

// A reasoning-capable provider streams the model's thinking BEFORE the answer text — the
// mock provider mirrors that ordering so streaming consumers behave identically under test.
streamedReasoning = ""
streamedAnswer    = ""

aiChatStream(
    "A farmer has 17 sheep. All but 9 die. How many are left?",
    ( chunk ) => {
        var reasoningPiece = chunk.choices?.first()?.delta?.reasoning ?: ""
        var contentPiece   = chunk.choices?.first()?.delta?.content ?: ""
        if ( len( reasoningPiece ) ) {
            streamedReasoning &= reasoningPiece
        }
        if ( len( contentPiece ) ) {
            streamedAnswer &= contentPiece
        }
    },
    {},
    {
        provider       : "mock",
        providerOptions: {
            responses: [
                {
                    content  : "9 sheep are left.",
                    reasoning: "Only the survivor count matters here — 9."
                }
            ]
        }
    }
)

println( "Streamed reasoning: " & streamedReasoning )
println( "Streamed answer   : " & streamedAnswer )
println( "" )

// ============================================================================
// Key Takeaways
// ============================================================================
println( "========================================" )
println( "KEY TAKEAWAYS:" )
println( "========================================" )
println( "1. Enabling reasoning is provider-specific and lives in params:" )
println( "   Claude -> thinking: { type: 'enabled', budget_tokens: N }" )
println( "   OpenAI -> reasoning_effort: 'low' | 'medium' | 'high'" )
println( "2. Reading it back is the SAME on every provider — the normalized envelope:" )
println( "   sync      -> choices[1].message.reasoning  (returnFormat: 'raw')" )
println( "   streaming -> chunk.choices?.first()?.delta?.reasoning" )
println( "3. Absence is normal — always guard with ?: '' " )
println( "4. Reasoning-capable providers stream thinking BEFORE the answer text" )
println( "5. The mock provider honors a scripted 'reasoning' key, so this whole read-side" )
println( "   pattern is testable offline with zero API keys" )
println( "" )
